## Why “processual”?

Because Śiva is not an inert underlying substance. Śiva exists inseparably from Śakti:

[
\text{manifest presence}
\equiv
\text{power of manifestation}.
]

Prakāśa without vimarśa would be an inert illumination incapable of differentiation. Vimarśa means that manifestation is intrinsically capable of:

* self-presentation;
* determination;
* articulation;
* memory;
* recognition;
* desire;
* action.

Spanda expresses the same anti-static commitment:

[
\boxed{
\text{the absolute is not behind activity;}
}
]

[
\boxed{
\text{its being consists in self-articulating activity.}
}
]

## Why “reflexive”?

Because consciousness does not become conscious through a second external act.

Its self-presence is intrinsic:

[
C\rightarrow R(C).
]

A cognition may subsequently become an object of reflection, but its original manifestation cannot depend on an infinite chain of further cognitions.

## Why “manifestation monism”?

Because subject and object are not two independently constituted substances.

They are differentiated poles of one appearing:

[
\text{aham}
\rightleftarrows
\text{idam}.
]

The five pure tattvas analyze possible weightings of that polarity:

[
\begin{aligned}
\text{Śiva}&:\quad \text{manifest subjectivity};\
\text{Śakti}&:\quad \text{power of articulation};\
\text{Sadāśiva}&:\quad I\text{-dominant “I am this”};\
\text{Īśvara}&:\quad this\text{-dominant “This am I”};\
\text{Śuddhavidyā}&:\quad balanced nonalienation.
\end{aligned}
]

The world is not outside manifestation, but neither is it merely an illusion inside a private mind.

It is:

[
\boxed{
\text{determinate manifestation}.
}
]

## Why “idealism” remains appropriate

Abhinavagupta does ultimately hold that all reality consists in or depends on universal consciousness. Matter is not a second ontological kind. It is maximally contracted and stabilized manifestation.

Therefore the closest established category remains:

[
\boxed{
\textbf{dynamic nondual idealism}.
}
]

But **reflexive manifestation monism** tells us more precisely what kind.

