# Final definition

I would now define the two theories as follows.

## Reflexive Manifestation Monism

> **Abhinavagupta’s metaphysics is a reflexive manifestation monism according to which reality is one intrinsically self-disclosing and self-articulating process whose powers generate subjectivity, objectivity, perspectival contraction, embodiment and material stability, and whose finite articulations can recognize their identity with the universal process.**

## Constructor-Theoretic Process Inexternalism

> **Process inexternalism is the view that one phenomenal field and one objectively individuated physical process are the intrinsic and extrinsic aspects of the same token event. Constructor theory describes the process’s possible transformations; aperture principles identify its complete carrier; and the inexternal identity postulate identifies that carrier with the phenomenal field without treating either as the cause of the other.**

